# =============================================================================
# Example crontab entries for the monthly PKN rebuild.
# Install with:  crontab -e   (then paste the relevant line and adjust paths)
# Inspect with:  crontab -l
# =============================================================================

# --- Option A: local / standalone server -------------------------------------
# Run at 03:00 on the 1st of every month, logging to a rotating file.
0 3 1 * *  /path/to/PKN_build_pipeline_opus4.8/schedule/run_monthly.sh >> /path/to/pkn_cron.log 2>&1

# --- Option B: HPC (PBS/Torque, e.g. VSC Ghent) ------------------------------
# The actual compute runs inside the PBS job; cron on the login node only
# submits it. Run at 03:00 on the 1st of every month.
# 0 3 1 * *  cd /path/to/PKN_build_pipeline_opus4.8 && qsub submit_pkn_hpc.sh >> /path/to/pkn_qsub.log 2>&1

# Notes:
#  * --resume (used inside run_monthly.sh) makes re-runs safe and incremental.
#  * If a run hits the HPC walltime, the next monthly attempt — or a manual
#    re-submit — finishes it, because completed databases are checkpointed.
